From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: display: rockchip: rk3528-vop: Allow the gamma LUT

The RK3528's VOP has a gamma lookup table for VP0 in a register window
of its own, as the RK3568's and RK3588's do: allow it as a second
register range, named gamma-lut.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/rockchip/rockchip,rk3528-vop.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/rockchip/rockchip,rk3528-vop.yaml
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/rockchip/rockchip,rk3528-vop.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/rockchip/rockchip,rk3528-vop.yaml
@@ -12,9 +12,15 @@
   compatible:
     const: rockchip,rk3528-vop
   reg:
-    maxItems: 1
+    minItems: 1
+    items:
+      - description: the registers
+      - description: VP0's gamma lookup table
   reg-names:
-    const: vop
+    minItems: 1
+    items:
+      - const: vop
+      - const: gamma-lut
   interrupts:
     minItems: 1
     maxItems: 4
